--> Polymorphism in java is an object oreinted programming concept where a single method or object can perform different behaviours based on the object that call it.
--> it allow one interface to be used for multiple forms of data.

polymorphism is acheived by using methodoverriding and upcasting
--> A parent class reference variable can refer to a child class object and java will automatically call the overriden method at run time. this is called dynamic method dispatch.

